# third_party/VENDOR.ndb: every vendored tree, checked by ./build vendor-check
# (ADR-0001, and upstream's ADR-0003 rules: pinned, reviewed source only).
# sha256= is the release tarball; an import from a source tree with no release
# has git.tree= instead, the directory's git tree id at the commit upstream=
# pins. tree.sha256= is the unpacked tree, as this prints inside it:
#   find . -type f -print0 | LC_ALL=C sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum | sha256sum
# subset= lists the parts of a larger release that were kept, paths as in the
# release; tree.sha256= is then over just those.

